msgid "The unread counter on the bell. Standard is the same 24px circle as the counters in the account menu, so every counter in your header reads as one family. Compact is the smaller 16px overlay earlier versions drew."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:139
msgid "Standard (24px, matches the menu counters)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:140
msgid "Compact (16px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:145
msgid "Nudge Sideways (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:146
msgid "Shifts the bell without moving anything else in your header: negative moves it left, positive right. Only needed if it does not quite line up with the buttons beside it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:156
msgid "Nudge Up or Down (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:157
msgid "Shifts the bell without moving anything else in your header: negative moves it up, positive down."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:167
msgid "Bell Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:168
msgid "The colour of the bell icon. Leave it empty to match the rest of your header. The unread count has its own colour, under Appearance."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:175
msgid "Bell Colour (Hover)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:176
msgid "The bell colour while pointed at or reached with the Tab key. Pick something clearly different from the colour above, so keyboard users can see where they are."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:183
msgid "Bell Background"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:184
msgid "The circle behind the bell icon. Leave it empty for no circle, which suits most headers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:191
msgid "Bell Background (Hover)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:192
msgid "The circle behind the bell while pointed at. Leave it empty for a soft shade that works on light and dark headers alike."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:199
msgid "Hide HivePress Counter"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:200
msgid "Hide the count HivePress shows in the header"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:201
msgid "HivePress shows its own combined count beside the account link, and in some themes on the menu button too. Ticking this hides it in both places and leaves only the bell's count, which covers the same events."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:208
msgid "Hide Messages Counter"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:209
msgid "Hide the unread count beside Messages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:210
msgid "Hides the count the Messages extension shows beside Messages in the account menu. It counts unread messages only, so keeping both is usually helpful. Without that extension this changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:217
msgid "Sticky Header"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:218
msgid "Keep the header on screen when scrolling"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:219
msgid "Keeps your whole site header at the top of the screen while people scroll, whether or not they are signed in. It follows the bell setting above, and leave it off if your theme already pins its header, or you will get two."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:226
msgid "Glass Effect"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:227
msgid "Let the page show through the pinned header"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:228
msgid "The pinned header becomes slightly see-through and blurs what scrolls behind it, and its dropdown menus get the same effect. Browsers that cannot blur, and anyone who has asked their device to reduce transparency, keep the solid header instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:235
msgid "Glass Opacity (%)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:236
msgid "How solid the pinned header stays. Lower lets more of the page through; below about 50 the text over it gets hard to read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:246
msgid "Glass Blur (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:247
msgid "How much the page behind the header is blurred. More blur hides the detail and keeps the header legible."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:264
msgid "Pinned Corner: Top Left (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:265
msgid "Rounds the top-left corner of the pinned header. 0 keeps it square."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:275
msgid "Pinned Corner: Top Right (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:276
msgid "Rounds the top-right corner of the pinned header. 0 keeps it square."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:286
msgid "Pinned Corner: Bottom Left (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:287
msgid "Rounds the bottom-left corner of the pinned header. 0 keeps it square."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:297
msgid "Pinned Corner: Bottom Right (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:298
msgid "Rounds the bottom-right corner of the pinned header. 0 keeps it square."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:309
msgid "Count how many notifications are sent and opened, as totals only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:314
msgid "Keeps sent and opened totals per notification type; nothing is recorded about individual people. While ticked, a Statistics page appears under HivePress. Unticking stops the counting and removes the page, keeping the totals collected so far."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:323
#: includes/configs/settings.php:329
msgid "Pop-ups"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:324
msgid "The small cards that slide in to announce a notification while someone is browsing. They only change the announcement; a notification nobody sees still waits on their notifications page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:330
msgid "Show new notifications as pop-ups"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:331
msgid "Untick and notifications still arrive; they wait on the notifications page, and on the bell if you have switched it on, instead of announcing themselves."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:338
msgid "Position"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:339
msgid "Which corner pop-ups appear in on desktops and laptops."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:347
msgid "Top Right"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:348
msgid "Top Left"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:349
msgid "Bottom Right"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:350
msgid "Bottom Left"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:355
msgid "Position on Mobile"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:356
msgid "Where pop-ups sit on screens narrower than 480 pixels; wider screens use the corner above. Pop-ups stretch the full width there, so only top, centre or bottom is possible."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:364
msgid "Top"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:365
msgid "Centre"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:366
msgid "Bottom"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:371
msgid "Maximum Pop-ups"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:372
msgid "How many pop-ups can be on screen at once. Any others wait their turn rather than piling up."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:383
msgid "Hiding"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:384
msgid "Hide pop-ups automatically"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:385
msgid "Untick to leave pop-ups on screen until they are closed by hand."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:393
msgid "Hide After (seconds)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:394
msgid "How long a pop-up stays before hiding itself; the countdown pauses while the pointer is on it. Allow long enough for a whole sentence. A missed pop-up still waits on the notifications page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:405
msgid "Sound"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:406
msgid "Play a sound with pop-ups"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:407
msgid "Browsers only allow sound after someone has clicked somewhere on the page, so the first pop-up of a visit may be silent. Later ones will chime."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:414
msgid "Sound Style"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:415
msgid "Which tone plays when a pop-up arrives."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:427
msgid "Chime"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:428
msgid "Ping"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:429
msgid "Pop"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:430
msgid "Bell"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:431
msgid "Soft"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:438
msgid "Appearance"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:442
msgid "Colours and sizing for notifications. Text size, weight, accent colour and icon shape apply everywhere notifications appear. Background, text colour and corner radius apply to the pop-ups and the bell dropdown only, because the notifications page uses your theme's own colours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:447
msgid "Background Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:448
msgid "The background of the pop-ups and the bell dropdown. Press Default beside the box to put the original white back; an empty box gives the same white."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:455
msgid "Text Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:456
msgid "The main text colour in the pop-ups and the bell dropdown. Keep it readable against the background above. Press Default to put the original near-black back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:463
msgid "Accent Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:464
msgid "The stripe on each pop-up, the unread dot, the links and the icon tile. Your brand colour usually suits. Press Default to put the original blue back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:471
msgid "Icon Shape"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:472
msgid "The shape of the small picture at the start of every notification, whether a profile photo, a listing photo or an icon. Circles suit sites about people; squares suit places or products."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:479
msgid "Circle"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:480
msgid "Rounded Square"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:481
msgid "Square"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:486
msgid "Corner Radius (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:489
msgid "How rounded the corners of the pop-ups and the bell dropdown are. 0 gives square corners; an empty box gives the standard 3px back instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:498
msgid "Button Radius (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:503
msgid "How rounded this extension's own buttons are, such as Mark all as read. 0 gives square corners; an empty box leaves them shaped like the other buttons in your theme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:511
msgid "Text Size (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:512
msgid "The size of notification text wherever it appears."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:521
msgid "Text Weight"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:522
msgid "How bold notification text is. Unread notifications are always bolder than read ones, whichever you pick."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:530
msgid "Medium"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:537
msgid "Unread Count Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:538
msgid "The small number on the bell and beside Notifications in the account menu. Left alone it matches the counts HivePress shows elsewhere; press Default to put that red back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:545
msgid "Dropdown Width (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:546
msgid "How wide the bell dropdown is on desktops and laptops; screens narrower than about 768 pixels use the full width instead. An empty box gives the standard 320."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:561
msgid "Types"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:570
msgid "Which notifications this plugin handles. Tick one and it appears on the notifications page, the bell and as a pop-up, with each person choosing how they receive it. Leave one unticked and this plugin ignores it: any email HivePress already sends carries on exactly as before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:579
msgid "Defaults"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:580
msgid "What each kind of user receives until they choose for themselves on their own Notification Settings page. On-site is the notification itself; Email decides only whether the email HivePress already sends still reaches them. Anyone who has saved that page keeps their own choice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:594
msgid "The wording and the title each notification shows on your site. Leave a box empty and the grey wording inside it is used, so only fill in what you want to change. Where the grey wording reads \"The email subject is used\", the subject line of the HivePress email is shown instead. A token is a placeholder between percent signs, such as %listing.title%, swapped for the real details when the notification is sent; hover the question mark beside a name to see the tokens it can use."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:612
msgid "Deleting Old Notifications"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:613
msgid "Older notifications can be deleted automatically as they build up. Nothing is deleted unless you fill in the box below, and it applies to everyone on your site, not only you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:620
msgid "Delete Notifications Older Than (days)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:621
msgid "Once a day, every notification older than this is deleted for good, for everyone, read or not, and it cannot be undone. An empty box means nothing is ever deleted. If unsure, start high, such as 365, and lower it later."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:635
#: includes/configs/settings.php:640
msgid "Performance Notifications"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:636
msgid "Once a night this compares each vendor with how they were doing, and tells them what changed: weekly views, a listing getting attention, a response rate moving. It needs Vendor Analytics Pro or Trust Signals to have anything to compare, runs as small background jobs, and never runs while a page is loading."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:641
msgid "Look for changes worth telling vendors about"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:642
msgid "Untick to stop the nightly comparison. The individual notifications stay listed under Types, and nothing already sent is removed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:648
msgid "Vendors Per Job"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:649
msgid "How many vendors each background job looks at before handing over to the next one. Smaller is gentler on a shared host; the default suits almost every site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:658
msgid "Vendors Per Night"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:659
msgid "The most vendors one night will look at, as a safety valve. With more vendors than this, the pass carries on from the same place the following night, so everyone is still reached."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:679
msgid "Removing the Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:680
msgid "Deleting this plugin keeps your notifications and settings, so you can reinstall and carry on; the warning WordPress shows on its delete screen is the same for every plugin and does not apply here. Switching the plugin off never removes anything. The box below is the one exception."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:685
msgid "Delete All Data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:686
msgid "Delete everything when this plugin is deleted"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:692
msgid "Leave this unticked unless you are certain. With it ticked, deleting the plugin also removes every notification, each person's delivery choices and quiet hours, the record of browsers allowed to show push, your wording and titles, your announcements, the Statistics totals and every setting on this page. It cannot be undone and nothing asks you to confirm at the time."
msgstr ""

